Not available: text color, images, video, quotes, code, horizontal line, indent buttons.

Default look (CSS): Times New Roman, 12 pt, double spacing.

Extra behavior (keyboard, paste, voice)
Tab (not in a list): first-line indent (five spaces as &nbsp;).
Shift+Tab: remove that indent.
Enter: next paragraph keeps the same indent (not for lists, headings, or center/right).
Paste from Word: indent and empty lines kept; fake Word bold/italic cleaned up.
Undo / redo: built-in history; page buttons use the same.
Dictation: inserts at the last caret so the mic does not jump the cursor.
Read-only: no toolbar.
Input format (into the editor)
Always an HTML string, never saved as Quill Delta.

Comes from	Format
Database
userContent HTML
Browser backup
Same HTML in localStorage
Word upload
Backend turns Word into Quill-like HTML, then the editor loads it
On load, empty paragraphs are forced to <p><br></p> so blank lines are not lost. Inside the session, HTML is converted to Quill’s Delta in memory only.

Output format (out of the editor)
Always HTML (innerHTML, then a small normalize).

Goes to	Format
Autosave / Save
HTML posted as { id, userContent }
Word count
HTML stripped to words
Download manuscript
Backend builds .docx from that HTML (ql-align-*, font-size, line-height, margin-bottom)
Olivia / Ellis
Backend strips HTML to plain text
Autosave waits 800ms after typing. “Unsaved” means the HTML (after normalize) differs from last saved.

Example of what gets stored:

<p class="ql-align-center" style="line-height: 2; margin-bottom: 12pt;">
  <span style="font-size: 12pt;">Chapter One</span>
</p>
<p>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;It was a dark and stormy night.</p>
